## Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
*.binlog
# NOT "[Dd]ebug/" or "[Rr]elease/", which the Visual Studio template puts here: those patterns
# match a directory of that name *anywhere*, so a source folder called Release — which is where
# the What's New page lives — is silently excluded from the repository, and the first sign of it
# is a clone that does not compile. Configuration output only ever lands under bin/ and obj/,
# which are already ignored above, so scoping them away costs nothing.

## Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml

## VSIX
# NOT "*.vsix": that pattern also matches the src/GitTabSync.Vsix *directory*, which silently
# excludes the entire extension project from the repository. Built packages only ever land in
# bin/, which is already ignored above.
*.pdb

## NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg
!packages/build/

## Rider / VS Code
.idea/
.vscode/
